  "summary": "Eleven items cluster on single-cell, spatial, and epitranscriptomic tooling and databases; none examine placenta or gestational diabetes.",
  "synthesis": "The observed activity is a cluster of computational tooling and resource papers spanning 3D genome modeling (U-Chrom), RNA editing quantification (OmniRE-seq), brain spatial proteomics segmentation (SPInfer, reporting segmentation F1 rising from 0.37 to 0.84), deep visual proteomics (OpenDVP), and segmentation benchmarking across 15 spatial transcriptomics datasets. Database resources include EvoNiche (91 matched datasets, 35 cancer types), scTHREAD (923,389 cells), 4D-atlas (1629 slices, 88 time points), and scSpatial (over 1800 sections). A review covers single-cell and spatial m6A epitranscriptomics, and a curated marker framework for early human developmental identity is validated across modalities. None of the items addresses placenta or gestational diabetes, so the category label does not match the evidence. The rise ratio of 3.29 is recorded from published and preprint counts only; no code or industry activity is observed, and no cause for the increase is attributable from these signals.",
